        "en": "The aerospace & defense sector encompasses a heterogeneous group of industries, spanning land and air weapons systems manufacturing, space defense including satellites and sensors, and air transport (both full-service and low-cost carriers). The sector comprises 36 listed companies with a combined market capitalization of approximately KRW 136.8 trillion, representing about 2.4% of the total market, with large-cap defense names dominating the sector's market-cap ranking. Hanwha Aerospace leads the sector overwhelmingly at KRW 51.92 trillion, followed by LIG Defense & Aerospace, Hyundai Rotem, Korea Aerospace Industries, and Hanwha Systems, giving the top five names an outsized weight. The air transport segment, including Korean Air, Asiana Airlines, and Jeju Air, carries comparatively smaller market capitalization relative to the defense names. In recent years, escalating geopolitical tensions have driven rising global defense demand, translating into overseas order wins and valuation re-rating for domestic manufacturers, structurally expanding the defense segment's weight within the sector."
