        "en": "A key point to monitor going forward is whether the execution of NCC capacity cuts translates into tangible profitability improvement; credit rating agencies note that the actual effects of restructuring will take considerable time to materialize and that near-term improvement in financial soundness remains difficult, suggesting normalization will be a gradual process. LG Chem plans to raise the sales mix of high-value petrochemical products—including EV-use synthetic rubber (SSBR), semiconductor-grade isopropyl alcohol (IPA), and ultra-high polymerization PVC—to above 25% by 2030, while simultaneously nurturing new growth businesses in semiconductor and mobility materials, making the pace of this specialty transition a key differentiator across companies within the sector. Emerging demand from data-center-related applications, such as high-value functional cooling fluids and immersion cooling technology validation, also warrants attention as a potential new market for chemical materials firms. Conversely, additional ethylene capacity coming online ahead of the S-Oil Shaheen project startup represents a supply-side offset that could partially counteract the impact of capacity reduction efforts. Whether contributions from new-industry materials segments—battery materials (cathodes, separators, electrolytes), solar, and fine chemicals—can offset weakness in commodity petrochemicals is likely to be the key factor distinguishing individual company performance."
